 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Interactive problem modelled with a simulated server holding secret in [1, upperBound]. check(g) returns \"PENDING\" on the first call and afterwards feedback about the previous call's guess: \"TOO_LOW\", \"TOO_HIGH\" or \"CORRECT\". Strategy: binary search with lo = 1, hi = upperBound; each round sets mid = floor((lo + hi) / 2) and calls check(mid) twice; the second answer is the feedback on mid (the first answer is ignored). Stop on \"CORRECT\". Return [found secret, total number of check calls].",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
